jobs=[('i1',(410,440),'The vertical canopy upright near the middle has a tiny horizontal step in its right dark outline, and the diagonal wooden rail has a broken white bevel at the horizontal artificial join. Repair those contour steps and unnatural horizontal material bands; keep all existing planks and paving.'),('i2',(1490,1440),'The right edge of the central crate upright has a tiny horizontal notch at the patch join. Continue its dark outline cleanly, maintaining original upright width. Remove rectangular wood/paving tone transitions without changing cargo crate or gray stone silhouettes.'),('i3',(2842,1400),'The diagonal curb behind the balustrade has a sliced triangular white bevel near the artificial horizontal join y~648. Restore one continuous thin bevel. The tall gray stone upright edges and far right quay edge have tiny horizontal steps at the same join; reconnect every existing outline exactly, preserve stone unit count and turquoise water.'),('i4',(980,2445),'The slim gray balustrade pillar near the middle has a tiny notch across the horizontal artificial join y~627. Make its vertical highlight and dark border continuous. Remove rectangular tone shifts in gray stone, without new cracks or extra slab seams.'),('i5',(2370,2445),'The gray quay face shows a horizontal material band and an irregular kink where the existing vertical panel groove crosses the artificial join y~627. Make this same groove a straight clean continuous line and keep existing rounded lower ends. Maintain wooden fender cap and all source geometry; do not add grooves.')]
